  "notes": "Only normal traffic ran, so every alert counts as a false positive. Alerts are read from the lab SOC and kept only if they are not duplicates, the flow ended no earlier than 10 s before the traffic began, both addresses are in 10.10.0.0/16 and the sensor is the lab sensor; the others are counted under reconciliation.excluded. Rates per activity are alerts per connection (about one flow each), matched by client port, server address:port and time from benign.sh's request lines; ssh, scp and ping have no known client port and match on address and time. The client is the attacker container (10.10.1.10), the address earlier attack runs used; the model keeps no state between flows, so that history does not affect the result. The lab round-trip time is about 0.1 ms, far below a real network's, so timing features (inter-arrival times, flow durations) are unrealistically short. The victim/client networks were not allowlisted, so false would-blocks show."
